A note on liquidation data, because most people don't know this.

When you see a liquidation total on any dashboard, you are mostly looking at samples and models, because most exchanges don't publish the real feed:

@binance : at most one liquidation per market per second.

@okx : their own documentation says the feed "doesn't represent the total number of liquidations."

@MEXC , @kucoincom : no public liquidation feed at all.

One major CEX does it right. Bybit's allLiquidation stream publishes every liquidation, across every contract, in 500 ms batches. That's the full ledger. Respect to @Bybit_Official for leading here.

On-chain perps already live at that standard - on Hyperliquid every liquidation, size and price is public by design.

Liquidations are the single most consequential event on a derivatives exchange. They move price, they move the whole market, and they happen to your account. There is no good reason a venue that liquidates its customers can't tell the market how much it liquidated.

@binance @okx and everyone else: publish the complete feed. Transparency here is not a feature request, it's the minimum.

We build https://t.co/wcD5xzm65t on whatever the exchanges give us. Give us the truth and we'll show it, instead of a predictive model.

